---
import { siteUrl } from '../../utils/site';
import Definition from '../../layouts/Definition.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../components/Mermaid.astro';
import AssetLoader from '../../components/screens/AssetLoader';
---

<Definition title="Download Content" section="Journey">
  <AssetLoader slot="preview" client:only="react" />

  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>Downloads the asset pack (size supplied by the bundled manifest) on first launch or when the pack version changes. Shows a progress bar only when the required pack needs downloading. An unchanged verified cache skips this screen.</p>

  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p>The in-app <code>assets_manifest.json</code> (bundled at build time) is the source of truth. It carries the pack's <code>sha256</code>, <code>size</code>, and <code>urls</code>.</p>
  <p>The cache path encodes the hash: <code>user://packs/assets-&lt;sha12&gt;.pck</code>. A successful verification and mount records a local receipt containing the full expected hash, byte size and file modification time. If the receipt still matches the file and manifest, bootstrap mounts without rescanning. A missing, malformed or mismatched receipt requires full SHA-256 verification. This is a local cache optimization, not protection against deliberate tampering that preserves file metadata. No separate metadata download is needed — the manifest is baked into the binary.</p>

  <Mermaid chart={`flowchart TD
    A[Bootstrap] --> B{Pack cached?}
    B -->|Receipt matches| G
    B -->|No valid receipt| C[Stream sha256 verify]
    C -->|Match| G[Mount pack]
    C -->|Mismatch| D[Delete stale, download]
    B -->|No file| D[Download from Arweave]
    D --> E[Write to user://packs/]
    E --> F[Stream sha256 verify]
    F -->|Match| G
    F -->|Mismatch| H[Fatal: integrity check failed]
    G --> I[Title Screen]
  `} />

  <h2>Cache cleanup</h2>
  <p>After a successful mount, any <code>*.pck</code> under <code>user://packs/</code> that doesn't match the current sha is deleted. Obsolete verification receipts are removed with their packs. The previous pack remains on disk until its replacement mounts successfully.</p>

  <h2>Error handling</h2>
  <p>The manifest lists multiple gateway URLs. Bootstrap tries each in order — if one fails, it falls through to the next. Total failure shows a message with a Retry action. Hash mismatch after download is also an error (no silent fallback). Retry clears the failed-host list and restarts preparation.</p>

  <h2>Previous</h2>
  <p><a href={siteUrl('/journey/splash')}>← Launch to Title</a></p>
  <h2>Next</h2>
  <p><a href={siteUrl('/journey/controls')}>Controls Setup →</a> (first run only)</p>
  <p><a href={siteUrl('/journey/title')}>Title Screen →</a> (subsequent launches)</p>
</Definition>
